reating the  products we crave  an increasing number of people are  choosing the profession in india  30 of students pursued a degree in stem  science technology engineering and  mathematics which produced almost 2.7  million graduates in 2018. where i live  in canada  enrollment in math computer and  information sciences has increased  47 comparing a recent academic year to  an earlier one  in a previous video i mentioned that  engineering degrees are now more common  than mba degrees amongst the world's top  performing  ceos which makes sense given some of the  biggest companies are tech giants  there's also the belief that engineers  rise to the top because they're good  problem solvers  google's former chief financial officer  patrick pichette once pointed out that  google is really an engineering company  with all these computer scientists that  see the world as a completely broken  place  engineers try to solve the most pressing  issues of the day using technology  musk is a self-taught engineer who wants  to reduce pollution with his electric  vehicles  and is confident the century-long  dominance of the internal combustion  engine  otherwise known as ice is coming to a  close well i don't think there will be  at ice industry long term  there's still like some steam engines  made somewhere but like they're just  basically  sort of quirky collector's items i mean  that will be the future of the internal  combustion engine car  at the same time people like him have  warned of a dark side to technology  he believes super intelligent machines  could pose a threat to humanity  and has called for government oversight  of artificial intelligence  fearing ai will surpass humans and  intelligence in the way we outsmart  cats smart machines are expected to  eliminate many human jobs  fedex has now teamed up with a robotics  company to test out autonomous delivery  vehicles  amazon runs cashier-less grocery stores  and wants to deliver packages by drone  in under 30 minutes  the world economic forum says the rise  of automation will result in a loss of  85 million jobs by 2025  yet in the same breath adds 97 million  new jobs will be created  such as ai and machine learning  specialists and data analysts  there's also the argument that future  technology will redefine the meaning of  the traditional work  week more than a hundred years ago  people worked 70 hours a week  on average with the industrial  revolution and labor laws it's now down  to about 35 hours  the former head of british petroleum  laura john brown remarked  why do we then define work as a 35 hour  a week why can't it be 17 and a half  behind these forces of societal change  are engineers  who dream big bezos space venture blue  origin has dreamt up space colonies  straight out of 70s science fiction  though the plan hasn't won over a fellow  billionaire who has a different vision  of humanity  in space musk spacex expects mars to be  colonized by a constant flow of humans  traveling aboard starships  so long as we have a desire for new  adventures and new things  engineers will continue to build the  future and enjoy all the attention that  comes along with it  at the core of an engineer is  exceptional skill and ability  if you'd like to brush up on your math  or computer science skills or you simply  want to learn more about how our world  works my sponsor brilliant can help  and it's free to sign up brilliant is a  website and app built off the principle  of learning while doing  you simply pick a course and jump right  in one of my favorites is the logic  courses  if you're feeling stuck on a problem you  can read the explanations to find out  more  brilliant has something for everybody  besides the math science and computer  science courses  you can even dive into cutting edge  topics like cryptocurrency  if you'd like to join me and a community  of 8 million learners and educators  click the link in my description  or visit brilliant.org newsthink the  firs